# What does this PR do?

This PR adds model card creation in case the `push_to_hub` argument is not used.

@patrickvonplaten

This PR further fixes nested lambda so that it's mature enough to be introduced into V's code.
You can feel functional programming's greater power on reducing code lines.

Before in scanner.v:
```V
mut is_generic := true
if s.last_lt >= 0 && s.pos - s.last_lt < 100 {
	typs := s.text[s.last_lt + 1..s.pos].split(',').map(it.trim_space().trim_right('>').after(']'))
	for typ in typs {
		if typ.len == 0 || (!(typ[0].is_capital() && typ[1..].bytes().all(it.is_alnum() || it == `_`)) && typ !in ast.builtin_type_names) {
	                is_generic = false
			break
		}
	}
} else {
	is_generic = false
}
```
After in scanner.v:
```V
is_generic := if s.last_lt >= 0 && s.pos - s.last_lt < 100 {
	typs := s.text[s.last_lt + 1..s.pos].split(',').map(it.trim_space().trim_right('>').after(']'))
	typs.all(it.len > 0 && ((it[0].is_capital() && it[1..].bytes().all(it.is_alnum() || it == `_`)) || it in ast.builtin_type_names))
} else {
	false
}
```
And actually with this PR the case could even be reduced into only one line! However for understandability I didn't do that.
```V
is_generic := s.last_lt >= 0 && s.pos - s.last_lt < 100 && s.text[s.last_lt + 1..s.pos].split(',').map(it.trim_space().trim_right('>').after(']')).all(it.len > 0 && ((it[0].is_capital() && it[1..].bytes().all(it.is_alnum() || it == `_`)) || it in ast.builtin_type_names))
```
